Core/Jessie: I saw military blockades when I was still at the station. What happened to them?
Core/Rose: They tried to quarantine the affected zones. Set up checkpoints, barriers.
Core/Jessie: Didn’t work?
Core/Rose: Hard to quarantine an airborne pollutant. The spores travel on the wind.
Core/Jessie: So the soldiers…
Core/Rose: Got infected like everyone else. Some of them are still out there. In uniform.
Core/Jessie: That’s… grim.
Core/Rose: Most things are now.